// The engine's own version, as opposed to the per-project "product version" in Build Settings
// (ProjectSettings::Build().Version), which belongs to the game a user ships.
//
// TARTARUS_GIT_DESCRIBE is captured at CONFIGURE time, not build time. That is deliberate: a
// custom command re-running `git describe` on every build would dirty the version header (and
// so relink the engine) on every commit, which costs more than it is worth for a string that
// only has to identify a release build. CI configures from a clean checkout, so a packaged
// build always carries the right SHA; a long-lived local build directory can show a stale one,
// which is why the About panel prints it next to the build date rather than on its own.

#define TARTARUS_VERSION_MAJOR @PROJECT_VERSION_MAJOR@
#define TARTARUS_VERSION_MINOR @PROJECT_VERSION_MINOR@
#define TARTARUS_VERSION_PATCH @PROJECT_VERSION_PATCH@
